{"title":"Pell's equation (simple solutions)","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Pell's equation is any Diophantine equation of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/7/fa788f10107a4f495516f787fc9f250b5d8b3f41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 – Dy^2 = 1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" />  where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is a given positive nonsquare integer,  and integer solutions are sought for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/e/56e228943301b048f242377b3b24717037d5996f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" />\n</p><p>Denote the sequence of solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22e85f5b2873c940dd42229c77568c422636bfe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_i, y_i \\}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" />\nIt is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/8/9081d9a71bb5b70c0fbeeec272e821fccf7a1b92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_0, y_0 \\} = \\{1,0 \\}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>During the solution we need:\n</p><p>a) to construct a recurrent sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57eadee256b564813c485d8427633f34531314d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_{i+1}, y_{i+1} \\} = f({x_i, y_i});$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"185\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>b) to prove that the equation has no other integer solutions.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Equation_of_the_form\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Equation of the form</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Equation_of_the_form_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Equation of the form</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Equation_of_the_form_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Equation of the form</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Pythagorean_triangles_with_almost_equal_legs\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Pythagorean triangles with almost equal legs</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Equation_of_the_form_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Equation of the form</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Equation_of_the_form_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Equation of the form</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Equation_of_the_form_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Equation of the form</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Equation_of_the_form_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Equation of the form</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Equation_of_the_form_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Equation of the form</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Equation_for_binomial_coefficients\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Equation for binomial coefficients</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Equation_of_the_form_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Equation of the form</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Equation_of_the_form\">Equation of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/f/2bfb0597ace1077ff545ca56072ff41958363a67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 2y^2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" /></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pell%27s_equation_(simple_solutions)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Equation of the form\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that all positive integer solutions of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/f/2bfb0597ace1077ff545ca56072ff41958363a67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 2y^2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" /> can be found using recursively transformation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/8/bb84c7f1aa3e192b5da95131360b422cce16e49e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{i+1} = 3 x_i + 4 y_i , y_{i+1} = 2 x_i + 3 y_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"264\" height=\"18\" /> of the pare <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76d03195412fa52541ad61a2ec8c0b1a8d44a058.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_0, y_0\\} = \\{1,0\\}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/4/a04ad9104d546aef29ce32246e260f3d80ad4616.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boldsymbol{a.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"10\" /> Let integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/f/3cfd2e221a809ef97d3152400e85f3cfe19d68b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_i, y_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> are the solution of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4ebe80d0817bb3e3159f75a1195306623cacbfec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hspace{10mm}   x_i^2 - 2 y_i^2 = 1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/1/4a1d3e1ca04d79d54a33c03b7477546d0bdfe68e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\begin{cases}  x_{i+1} &amp;= 3 x_i + 4 y_i ,\\\\ y_{i+1} &amp;= 2 x_i + 3 y_i .   \\end{cases} \\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"53\" />\nThen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/7/327e33710da5329c7622318d658827062d605c50.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_{i+1}^2 - 2 y_{i+1}^2 = (3 x_i + 4 y_i)^2 - 2 (2 x_i + 3 y_i)^2 =  x_i^2 - 2 y_i^2 = 1.\\]\" width=\"462\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Therefore integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e07d47a2f54b7016607fd889e7c9e58ab44bf30e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_{i+1}, y_{i+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> are the solution of the given equation. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25dfa5e1205b2ae736cbc053851e5518ca1d554e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/9/ce9c0bfffee6d193577e884027a7cd26e5074412.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_{i+1} &gt; y_{i+1}  \\ge 2(x_i + y_i) &gt; x_i &gt; y_i &gt; 0.\\]\" width=\"303\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/0/fe0fe7e0c16fee2797c23575c50517bc4d37a038.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\{(x_i, y_i) \\} = \\{(1,0), (3,2), (17,12), (99,70), (577,408), (3363, 2738),...\\}.\\]\" width=\"548\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/7/e37667e649506d83bafb06bab773e8b8e38e4b6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boldsymbol{b.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> Suppose that the pare of the positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/0/8e047bc273bde20580246888392761fc3e34a54e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_j, y_j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> is the solution different from founded in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/4/a04ad9104d546aef29ce32246e260f3d80ad4616.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boldsymbol{a.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"10\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/b/b5b87c2337403b8d473f99b7323561829c3225af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_j^2 - 2 y_j^2 = 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"106\" height=\"24\" /> Let\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/6/7c6560697f123dbd995e9a43d81e310aa9532638.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\begin{cases}  x_{i+1} &amp;= 3 x_i - 4 y_i ,\\\\ y_{i+1} &amp;= - 2 x_i + 3 y_i .   \\end{cases} \\]\" width=\"169\" height=\"53\" />\nthen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5ab286d8cf99122585b735f4678e453572fdb554.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{i+1}^2 - 2 y_{i+1}^2 = (3 x_i - 4 y_i)^2 - 2 (-2 x_i + 3 y_i)^2 =  x_i^2 - 2 y_i^2 = 1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"480\" height=\"23\" />\ntherefore integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e07d47a2f54b7016607fd889e7c9e58ab44bf30e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_{i+1}, y_{i+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> are the solution of the given equation.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/9/3793bbeadc79e21cc6ade6306ac91a48f2fb4bfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i^2 = 2 y_i^2 +1 &gt;  2 y_i^2 \\implies  x_i &gt; y_i &gt;0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"294\" height=\"21\" /> Similarly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/e/3ee5b959404a997212960c5926bfb3c35d85d331.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{i +1}&gt; y_{i+1}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>There is no integer solution if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/9143aae34207a6753333a019ea98041cd42aa04d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_j = 1. y_j = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"105\" height=\"19\" /> is impossible. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/8/4183039b3f39b2944d3d85787eaf826d29a12383.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_i &gt; 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/e/63e11583d49b47ecd42c4f86b8376054d373f9c3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9 y_i^2 \\ge 8 y_i^2 + 4  = 4 x_i^2 \\implies 3y_i \\ge 2x_i  \\implies y_{i+1} \\ge 0.\\]\" width=\"398\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/b/bfbc2f25da1f9fc911fef97bcc69a2e65b8b7044.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0 \\le y_{i+1} = y_i - 2 (x_i - y_i) &lt; y_i.\\]\" width=\"243\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>There is no member <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/e/1ee9e9f0e92c3d5d278ad9b5be0a5e5872c9a5d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_j  = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"17\" /> in the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/0/8c019a668bb82449ac7f7b244372fecc7fbce3f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{y_i \\},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> hence it is infinitely decreasing sequence of natural numbers. There is no such sequence. Contradiction.\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Equation_of_the_form_2\">Equation of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1e76997a4cd43ff3e9fcfb986a89d3a74b79be6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x + 1) = 2y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"21\" /></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pell%27s_equation_(simple_solutions)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Equation of the form\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that all positive integer solutions of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1e76997a4cd43ff3e9fcfb986a89d3a74b79be6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x + 1) = 2y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"21\" /> can be found using recursively transformation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/8/e58ae06c225a30dd820b83294cac6ff43a00ece9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{i+1} = 3 x_i + 4 y_i + 1, y_{i+1} = 2 x_i + 3 y_i + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"327\" height=\"18\" /> of the pare <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/8/168aeb028ee256611efbaa3f7c8e4a0418e7b15a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_0, y_0\\} = \\{0,0\\}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" /> In another form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e31570a11af702affbcfc29e27a6b445a8e905.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x_{i+1}} = \\sqrt{2x_i} + \\sqrt{x_i + 1}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"204\" height=\"23\" /> \n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/d/cbd524070be6b15665c850619cbce96a26d589db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x(x + 1) = 2y^2 \\implies 4x^2 + 4x + 1 = 8y^2 + 1 \\implies (2x+1)^2 - 2(2y)^2 = 1.\\]\" width=\"529\" height=\"20\" />\nIt is the form of Pell's equation, therefore\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb8e793b1c94b236199e8e4cf40d59a551b12ee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\begin{cases} 2x_{i+1}+1 &amp;= 3 (2x_i + 1)+ 4 (2y_i) ,\\\\ 2y_{i+1} &amp;= 2 (2x_i + 1) +3 (2y_i) .   \\end{cases} \\]\" width=\"273\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/8/8a8ab052a316f83a48dee6309826a63c9d0178f6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\begin{cases} x_{i+1} &amp;= 3x_i + 4y_i + 1,\\\\ y_{i+1} &amp;= 2x_i + 3y_i + 1.   \\end{cases} \\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/8/9482a0a567ba0d4ae918f326c42982429c1732f4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c}  &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2ex] \\boldsymbol{i} &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; 2 &amp; 3 &amp; 4 &amp; 5 &amp; 6 &amp; 7 \\\\ [0.5ex] \\hline   &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-1.5ex]  \\boldsymbol{x_i} &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; 8 &amp; 49 &amp; 288 &amp; 1681 &amp; 9800 &amp; 57121 \\\\ [1ex]      \\boldsymbol{y_i} &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; 6 &amp; 35 &amp; 204 &amp; 1189 &amp; 1681 &amp; 40391 \\\\ [1ex]     \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"359\" height=\"93\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/b/8db56426ba62c775fc12ac1eb97e13c9ca82ccb8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_{i+1} = 3 x_i + 4 y_i + 1 = 2x_i + 2 \\sqrt {2 x_i (x_i + 1)} + (x_i + 1) = (\\sqrt {2x_i} + \\sqrt{x_i + 1})^2\\]\" width=\"547\" height=\"32\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/a/58a0542b6edc1b6a6c73b06108d179253b8fff26.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\sqrt{x_{i+1}}= \\sqrt{2x_i} + \\sqrt{x_i + 1}.\\]\" width=\"238\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Equation_of_the_form_3\">Equation of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/e/afeadf4464f7115035e340bca5b72add7b3a9e2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 2y^2 = - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"20\" /></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pell%27s_equation_(simple_solutions)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Equation of the form\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that all positive integer solutions of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/8/c58e0b58acfe1705c2ce9b17a2c0b765f90d0a77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 2y^2 = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" /> can be found using recursively transformation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/1/4a1d3e1ca04d79d54a33c03b7477546d0bdfe68e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\begin{cases}  x_{i+1} &amp;= 3 x_i + 4 y_i ,\\\\ y_{i+1} &amp;= 2 x_i + 3 y_i .   \\end{cases} \\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"53\" />\nof the pare <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/c/74c27b6a79a9c5de986dc3e849fa05a765fd3eb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_0, y_0\\} = \\{1,1\\}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p>The solution is similar to that discussed in the previous section.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/4/e742939a8a1a072d9981190323e5687195b1983d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c}  &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2ex] \\boldsymbol{i} &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; 2 &amp; 3 &amp; 4 &amp; 5 &amp; 6 \\\\ [0.5ex] \\hline   &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-1.5ex]  \\boldsymbol{x_i} &amp; 1 &amp; 7 &amp; 41 &amp; 239 &amp; 1393 &amp; 8119 &amp; 47321 \\\\ [1ex]      \\boldsymbol{y_i} &amp; 1 &amp; 5 &amp; 29 &amp; 169 &amp; 985 &amp; 5741 &amp; 33461 \\\\ [1ex]     \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"333\" height=\"93\" />\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Pythagorean_triangles_with_almost_equal_legs\">Pythagorean triangles with almost equal legs</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pell%27s_equation_(simple_solutions)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Pythagorean triangles with almost equal legs\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all triangles with integer sides one leg of which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than the other.\n</p><p>Find all natural solutions of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/3/6a3099a7f00f18c73606a1b69a5ca3aa83777a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + (x+1)^2 = y^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Solution</b></i>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb83d0a3dbfb57f34c50a40afa9507e7a54a5c8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 +(x + 1)^2 = 2x^2 + 2x + 1 = y^2 \\implies 4x^2 + 4x + 1 = 2y^2 - 1 \\implies (2x+1)^2 - 2y^2 = -1.\\]\" width=\"647\" height=\"20\" />\nAll positive integer solutions of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/d/d1dc2b76ed657d46d551f978289845f8de3c7b78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2x+1)^2 - 2y^2 = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"170\" height=\"21\" /> can be found using recursively transformation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/5/535e32152747739cbec065997f93aaceaa78f1b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\begin{cases}  2x_{i+1}+1 &amp;= 3 (2x_i + 1) + 4 y_i ,\\\\ y_{i+1} &amp;= 2(2x_i + 1) + 3 y_i .  \\end{cases} \\]\" width=\"250\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82d0615193d3832d8570d23c1aad00ea4e032efc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\begin{cases} x_{i+1} &amp;= 3x_i + 2y_i + 1 ,\\\\ y_{i+1} &amp;= 4x_i + 3y_i + 2 . \\end{cases} \\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"53\" />\nof the pare <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/e/fae6eb2eb41e20b1e76e3b671abcc29613750a0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_0, y_0\\} = \\{0,1\\}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/e/81ea0890aafb7f1d29b75b1dadf780a316201545.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c|c|c|c}  &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2ex] \\boldsymbol{i} &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; 2 &amp; 3 &amp; 4 &amp; 5 \\\\ [0.5ex] \\hline   &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-1.5ex]  \\boldsymbol{x_i} &amp; 0 &amp; 3 &amp; 20 &amp; 119 &amp; 696 &amp; 4059 \\\\ [1ex]      \\boldsymbol{y_i} &amp; 1 &amp; 5 &amp; 29 &amp; 169 &amp; 985 &amp; 5741 \\\\ [1ex]     \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"262\" height=\"93\" />\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Equation_of_the_form_4\">Equation of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/0/930e39738b21b10ce9bdb8dbf997729b55a3c2c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 3y^2 = - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"20\" /></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pell%27s_equation_(simple_solutions)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Equation of the form\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/c/d2c6e811656e162b72618ec9815b52a5a113c5a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 3y^2 = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" /> have not any solution.\n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/5/dd5c3083f4844b5f647cadc7518e3d89d67b438c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = 3k \\implies x^2 \\pmod{3}= 0.\\]\" width=\"239\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/1/e012a36485c1776c8c9d376f0ad040c1685fb638.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = 3k \\pm 1 \\implies x^2 \\pmod{3}= 1.\\]\" width=\"271\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/8/f9828df495c90ff4336f139f4af066862501eaf8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(- 3y^2 + 1) \\pmod {3} = 1 \\implies (x^2 - 3y^2 + 1) \\pmod {3} = \\{1, 2 \\} \\ne 0 \\implies\\]\" width=\"559\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/e/dae8a08fbe68166512b96e8eb336ece0f06be55f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 - 3y^2 + 1 \\ne 0.\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"19\" />\n<b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Equation_of_the_form_5\">Equation of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/4/8b4f4919741185e69f8556b98c7940b0dc02e6dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 2y^2 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" /></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pell%27s_equation_(simple_solutions)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Equation of the form\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that all positive integer solutions of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/4/8b4f4919741185e69f8556b98c7940b0dc02e6dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 2y^2 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" /> can be found using recursively transformation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/685ce8052b1c8e4d45ed9f3e07305c7e07147004.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\begin{cases} x_{i+1} &amp;= 3 x_i + 4 y_i ,\\\\ y_{i+1} &amp;= 2 x_i + 3 y_i . \\end{cases} \\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"53\" />\nof the pares <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/f/3afa897eb381f8dcede03bd4c28646285b43512c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_1, y_1\\} = \\{3,1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/4119bb38597b19bd1155ca061d3643a552c81a0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{\\hat{x}_1, \\hat{y}_1 \\} = \\{5,3\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/4/a04ad9104d546aef29ce32246e260f3d80ad4616.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boldsymbol{a.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"10\" /> Let integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/f/3cfd2e221a809ef97d3152400e85f3cfe19d68b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_i, y_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> are the solution of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/348146bbfc5829a16ce7f4c8447ddc6bb76b6391.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hspace{10mm}   x_i^2 - 2 y_i^2 = 7,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/685ce8052b1c8e4d45ed9f3e07305c7e07147004.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\begin{cases} x_{i+1} &amp;= 3 x_i + 4 y_i ,\\\\ y_{i+1} &amp;= 2 x_i + 3 y_i . \\end{cases} \\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/0/810a1da47b85402adce3015a8132d79b924ff9d5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_{i+1}^2 - 2 y_{i+1}^2 = (3 x_i + 4 y_i)^2 - 2 (2 x_i + 3 y_i)^2 =  x_i^2 - 2 y_i^2 = 7.\\]\" width=\"462\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Therefore integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e07d47a2f54b7016607fd889e7c9e58ab44bf30e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_{i+1}, y_{i+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> are the solution of the given equation.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/9/ce9c0bfffee6d193577e884027a7cd26e5074412.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_{i+1} &gt; y_{i+1}  \\ge 2(x_i + y_i) &gt; x_i &gt; y_i &gt; 0.\\]\" width=\"303\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/f/b2f3699d5e310d5eddf34785a7cd2e87ce741e03.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c|c|c}  &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2ex] \\boldsymbol{i} &amp; 1 &amp; 2 &amp; 3 &amp; 4 &amp; 5 \\\\ [0.5ex] \\hline   &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-1.5ex]  \\boldsymbol{x_i} &amp; 3 &amp; 13 &amp; 75 &amp; 437 &amp; 2547 \\\\ [1ex]      \\boldsymbol{y_i} &amp; 1 &amp; 9 &amp; 53 &amp; 309 &amp; 1801 \\\\ [1ex]     \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"227\" height=\"93\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/7/e37667e649506d83bafb06bab773e8b8e38e4b6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boldsymbol{b.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> The pare of the positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/6/6566dda11991f0724034b89ce2772773288033e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\hat {x}_i, \\hat{y}_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"54\" height=\"20\" /> is the solution different from founded in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/4/a04ad9104d546aef29ce32246e260f3d80ad4616.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boldsymbol{a.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"10\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/1/9912636cbcfab1cbd4dca91bae3991398d499169.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hat {x}_i^2 - 2 \\hat {y}_i^2 = 7.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"21\" /> Let\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/f/3af45f63ee9927390e155e8672d4af8e92dddd63.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\begin{cases} \\hat{x}_{i+1} &amp;= 3  \\hat{x}_i - 4  \\hat{y}_i ,\\\\ \\hat{y}_{i+1} &amp;= - 2  \\hat{x}_i + 3  \\hat{y}_i . \\end{cases} \\]\" width=\"169\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/3/113043b644f60f350f67594b5588fc9ffddbb329.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\hat{x}_{i+1}^2 - 2  \\hat{y}_{i+1}^2 = (3  \\hat{x}_i - 4  \\hat{y}_i)^2 - 2 (-2  \\hat{x}_i + 3  \\hat{y}_i)^2 =   \\hat{x}_i^2 - 2  \\hat{y}_i^2 = 7,\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"21\" />\ntherefore integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5dbf41967bddc6119606dd379a6838869adc1811.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$( \\hat{x}_{i+1},  \\hat{y}_{i+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" /> are the solution of the given equation.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/8/ba87904da49311a4c005bff43b694edca84e9272.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hat{x}_i^2 = 2 \\hat{y}_i^2 +1 &gt;  2 \\hat{y}_i^2 \\implies \\hat{x}_i &gt; \\hat{y}_i &gt; 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"294\" height=\"21\" /> Similarly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb35e8ff73f7d70b9d7613c7139bd93e6b6176d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hat{x}_{i +1} &gt; \\hat{y}_{i+1}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/4/9b4c1af4c331c624996c945c865670df93978fb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hat{y}_i &gt; 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/1/cf14194cf95c09db1aea0011dc72147a399fd94e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9 \\hat{y}_i^2 \\ge 8 \\hat{y}_i^2 + 28  = 4 \\hat{x}_i^2 \\implies 3 \\hat{y}_i \\ge 2 \\hat{x}_i  \\implies \\hat{y}_{i+1} \\ge 0.\\]\" width=\"407\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/563d654278b0ffc5bb35b091398acf400c90200e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0 \\le \\hat{y}_{i+1} = \\hat{y}_i - 2 (\\hat{x}_i – \\hat{y}_i) &lt;\\hat{y}_i.\\]\" width=\"230\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>There is no member <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/3/9b36359acc3510c0995906028898fd5474e3de31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hat{y}_j  = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"51\" height=\"19\" /> in the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/5/cf59328ad63846ea23b070969a1c48ad18e936ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{\\hat{y}_i \\},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> hence it is infinitely decreasing sequence of natural numbers. There is no such sequence. Contradiction.\n</p><p>We need to check <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/7/167e20c4065909cea50de82ed34eb44a4319e0a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hat{y}_j = \\{2,4,5\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" /> (no solution), but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/8/ee88607d6e3ed08e03f266565bb13ea8416bd588.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hat{y}_j = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"51\" height=\"19\" /> gives the integer solution, so there is the second sequence of the integer solutions\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/0/8c0c8b191a5ceea4a106471dc395338ca9390214.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c|c|c}  &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2ex] \\boldsymbol{i} &amp; 1 &amp; 2 &amp; 3 &amp; 4 &amp; 5 \\\\ [0.5ex] \\hline   &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-1.5ex]  \\boldsymbol{\\hat{x}_i} &amp; 5 &amp; 27 &amp; 157 &amp; 915 &amp; 5333 \\\\ [1ex]      \\boldsymbol{\\hat{y}_i} &amp; 3 &amp; 19 &amp; 111 &amp; 647 &amp; 3771 \\\\ [1ex]     \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"236\" height=\"93\" />\n<b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Equation_of_the_form_6\">Equation of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/1/ea1369242a81ef9899400339e72712265c41cd60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - xy - y^2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" /></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pell%27s_equation_(simple_solutions)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Equation of the form\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that all positive integer solutions of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/1/ea1369242a81ef9899400339e72712265c41cd60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - xy - y^2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/1/5612ecfb5290d83ad05ced683abc38f9b357a950.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_i, y_i \\} = \\{F_{2i +1}, F_{2i}\\}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"178\" height=\"20\" /> They can be found using recursively transformation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/3/883a7faecb60fd16b6d74d7b8bc461feb65dfc35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_{i+1} = x_i + y_i , x_{i+1} = 2x_i + y_i = y_{i+1} + x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"330\" height=\"18\" /> of the pares <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76d03195412fa52541ad61a2ec8c0b1a8d44a058.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_0, y_0\\} = \\{1,0\\}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/d/58d6bbf30d15ba90def498719762bde623bbe286.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 - xy - y^2 = 1 \\implies 4x^2 - 4xy + y^2 - 5y^2 = 1 \\implies (2x+y)^2 - 5y^2 = 1.\\]\" width=\"531\" height=\"20\" />\nLet the pare of the positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/f/3cfd2e221a809ef97d3152400e85f3cfe19d68b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_i, y_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> be the solution of given equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb1df488754f82055d970153be08d13d1d61edc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i^2 - x_i y_i - y_i^2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"21\" /> and  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/b/63b47e5accc8dd915bfe21aadfba6a18a89a0d05.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\begin{cases} x_{i+1} &amp;= 2x_i + y_i ,\\\\ y_{i+1} &amp;= x_i + y_i .  \\end{cases} \\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"53\" />\nThen\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/7046692967ef867a8fe26aa14b2eb4f5af84d570.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_{i + 1}^2 - x_{i + 1} y_{i + 1} - y_{i + 1}^2 = x_i^2 - x_i y_i - y_i^2 = 1.\\]\" width=\"342\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/8/548152ba4dda8771ef54213493951ffafba9cffd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c}  &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2ex] \\boldsymbol{i} &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; 2 &amp; 3 &amp; 4 &amp; 5 &amp; 6 &amp; 7 \\\\ [0.5ex] \\hline   &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-1.5ex]  \\boldsymbol{x_i} &amp; 1 &amp; 2 &amp; 5 &amp; 13 &amp; 34 &amp; 89 &amp; 233 &amp; 610 \\\\ [1ex]      \\boldsymbol{y_i} &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; 3 &amp; 8 &amp; 21 &amp; 55 &amp; 144 &amp; 377 \\\\ [1ex]     \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"304\" height=\"93\" />\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Equation_of_the_form_7\">Equation of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/7/527ca3698f4c82f398d6466f886fedf09f792e4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - xy - y^2 = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"20\" /></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pell%27s_equation_(simple_solutions)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Equation of the form\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that all positive integer solutions of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/7/527ca3698f4c82f398d6466f886fedf09f792e4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - xy - y^2 = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"20\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/7/86755ab3b50d8ef4918998ce69221912b2d857bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_i, y_i \\} = \\{F_{2i}, F_{2i-1}\\}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" /> They can be found using recursively transformation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03ccd625bba6064616c8cbe6180b24c6b5520278.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\begin{cases} x_{i+1} &amp;= 2x_i + y_i = y_{i+1} + x_i,\\\\ y_{i+1} &amp;= x_i + y_i .  \\end{cases} \\]\" width=\"239\" height=\"53\" />\nof the pares <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e420886fb69f40bf956c6a65528d06bf7b4ac8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_0, y_0\\} = \\{1,1\\} = \\{F_1, F_2 \\}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"225\" height=\"20\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/0/c6006671338fbad31d3a4e597a18659e75f4805c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c}  &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2ex] \\boldsymbol{i} &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; 2 &amp; 3 &amp; 4 &amp; 5 &amp; 6 &amp; 7 \\\\ [0.5ex] \\hline   &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-1.5ex]  \\boldsymbol{x_i} &amp; 1 &amp; 3 &amp; 8 &amp; 21 &amp; 55 &amp; 144 &amp; 377 &amp; 987 \\\\ [1ex]      \\boldsymbol{y_i} &amp; 1 &amp; 2 &amp; 5 &amp; 13 &amp; 34 &amp; 89 &amp; 233 &amp; 610 \\\\ [1ex]     \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"313\" height=\"93\" />\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Equation_of_the_form_8\">Equation of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/6/806d0aaa8d61c2e8d0f966b2d4a9234ce754f97e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 5y^2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" /></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pell%27s_equation_(simple_solutions)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Equation of the form\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that all positive integer solutions of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/6/806d0aaa8d61c2e8d0f966b2d4a9234ce754f97e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 5y^2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/2/9520a4c4e1866ccedf47a9813cd5d7b7a9f368b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\{x_i, y_i \\} = \\{F_{2i+1} + F_{2i - 1}, F_{2i}\\}.\\]\" width=\"237\" height=\"18\" />\nIt is clear that solutions can be found using recursively transformation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/f/68f176ce95800b6a7147cd6ea5523acf58dd5b91.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\begin{cases} x_{i+1} = \\frac {3x_i }{2}+ \\frac {5y_i }{2},\\\\ y_{i+1} = \\frac {x_i }{2}+ \\frac {3y_i }{2}  \\end{cases} \\]\" width=\"141\" height=\"53\" /> \nof the pare <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/b/49b0c93df75831233b1730c3cbadb9d683553dcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_1, y_1\\} = \\{3, 1\\} = \\{F_3 +F_1, F_2\\}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"266\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>One can use the small transform for understanding \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/e/ebe3aeb748079aa6b6a3eda8b4ea30a790987f95.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_{i + 1} - y_{i + 1} = x_i + y_i = (x_i - y_i) + 2y_i  \\Rightarrow 2F_{2i+1} = 2F_{2i-1} + 2F_{2i}, x_1-y_1 = 2F_1.\\]\" width=\"578\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/2/ba2700a7139f9139f39656c166adffd4feaa87fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y_{i + 1} = \\frac {x_i - y_i}{2}+ 2 y_i   \\Rightarrow    F_{2i +2} = F_{2i-1} + 2F_{2i} =  F_{2i+1} + F_{2i}, y_1 = F_2.\\]\" width=\"504\" height=\"33\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/b/ccbffb5b37c9b25b2a97719714f3a98d90ed55fa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c}  &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2ex] \\boldsymbol{i} &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; 2 &amp; 3 &amp; 4 &amp; 5 &amp; 6 &amp; 7 \\\\ [0.5ex] \\hline   &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-1.5ex]  \\boldsymbol{x_i} &amp; 3 &amp; 7 &amp; 18 &amp; 47 &amp; 123 &amp; 322 &amp; 377 &amp; 843 \\\\ [1ex]      \\boldsymbol{y_i} &amp; 1 &amp; 3 &amp; 8 &amp; 21 &amp; 55 &amp; 89 &amp; 144 &amp; 377 \\\\ [1ex]     \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"331\" height=\"93\" />\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Equation_for_binomial_coefficients\">Equation for binomial coefficients</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pell%27s_equation_(simple_solutions)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Equation for binomial coefficients\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all positive integer solutions of equation  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/9/e79b9e875e0d135e05ea0bdf60158fd1357c47a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{x}{y-1} = \\binom{x-1}{y}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"170\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Solution</b></i>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/3/22350e09d8ca7b0db0791ed18485f3a8bc80306a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\binom{x}{y-1} = \\frac{x!}{(y-1)!(x-y+1)!}, \\binom{x-1}{y} = \\frac{(x-1)!}{y!(x-y-1)!} \\implies\\]\" width=\"498\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/7/aa716fbef0a3213afa1a185833ec33e36f73f91b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[xy=(x-y+1) \\cdot (x-y) \\implies x^2 -3xy +y^2 +x - y = 0.\\]\" width=\"460\" height=\"20\" />\nIt is known that every real quadratic form under a linear change of variables may be transformed in a \"diagonal form\".\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/b/68b70584b587a08440f55e5d1bc80c02b40024e6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x + \\frac {1}{5})^2 + (y - \\frac {1}{5})^2 - 3 (x + \\frac {1}{5})(y - \\frac {1}{5}) = \\frac {1}{5},\\]\" width=\"346\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/b/96bfb7d11ae968fc6c6a5e5f39f3bc74c3940aee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(5y - 1)^2 - 5 (2x - 3y + 1)^2 = - 4,\\]\" width=\"266\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/726639b72a9e42a99617f33c74f6e2891f83ab37.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[u = 5y - 1, v = 2x - 3y + 1 \\implies u^2 - 5 v^2 = - 4 \\implies\\]\" width=\"419\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/0/500fe1d38f26cc3e3ea619e22d76c9447f7c7dfc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\begin{cases} u_i = 5y_i - 1 = F_{2i} + F_{2i - 2},\\\\ v_i = 2x_i - 3y_i + 1 = F_{2i-1}. \\end{cases} \\]\" width=\"222\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/f/09fb3d5cff603bab56022842fbc55e1e0fd08eb6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y_i = \\frac {F_{2i} + F_{2i - 2} + 1}{5} = \\frac {L_{2i - 1} + 1}{5},\\]\" width=\"265\" height=\"37\" /> where L is Lucas number,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/2/3426423fe9d25d1ca31dfcca87597b92c33e141e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_0 = 2, L_1 = 1, L_i = F_{i-1} + F_{i+1} = L_i + L_{i - 1}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"361\" height=\"18\" />\nIt is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/4/c24bfd42635296a036336d05060732f37a5e822f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\{L_i \\} = \\{2,1,3,4,\\hspace{5mm}   7,11,18,29, \\hspace{5mm}  47,...\\}\\]\" width=\"329\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e0e9b0e21f8d9aba2b39f250636c22f3f586e7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\{L_i \\pmod 5 \\} = \\{2,1,3,4, \\hspace{5mm} 2,1,3,4,\\hspace{5mm} 2,...\\}\\]\" width=\"375\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/d/c4d9c3fe2486718236551597878d29f2f2516f49.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[L_i \\pmod 5 = (L_{i-1} \\pmod 5 + L_{i-2} \\pmod 5 ) \\pmod 5 = L_{i+4} \\pmod 5,\\]\" width=\"614\" height=\"18\" /> \nso sequence of Lucas numbers modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is periodic, the period is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/4054552638cf9f29e857a1306bd3ec31df3c19b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> and the numbers with index <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/f/9bf07d5fa375c78e707642715b140e8b8ee7440e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4i-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" /> (only these numbers) are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b835f2c6c592edc4583ce996f86bcc0d07ca8da5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Therefore only numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/e/66ec1db85ec834ed4c8a4b9a52954aa86ea57787.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y_i = \\frac {F_{4i} + F_{4i – 2} + 1}{5}\\]\" width=\"154\" height=\"37\" /> are integer.\n</p><p>We use the identities <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/e/b3e8c04ea49ca48cd1d0daae32aeb23fc59ac960.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[F_{2i-1}^2- F_{2i} \\cdot F_{2i-2} = 1, F_{4i} = F_{2i} (F_{2i+1} + F_{2i-1}), F_{4i – 2} = F_{2i-1}(2F_{2i} - F_{2i-1})\\]\" width=\"558\" height=\"20\" /> and get  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/3/3d36e0f38cd1d53a2760573e7a4aede847fdaf53.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y_i = F_{2i} F_{2i-1}.\\]\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>We use the identities <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1f4c979444ee395b15cf4d7a362997b2a43fecb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[F_{4i-1}= F_{2i}^2 + F_{2i-1}^2, F_{2i-1}^2 - F_{2i} \\cdot F_{2i-2} = 1,\\]\" width=\"337\" height=\"20\" />\nand get \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/5/6b58f7c329836088eaae22c3b74c391d4740650f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_i = \\frac{ 3y_i - 1 + F_{4i-1}}{2} =  \\frac{ F_{2i}(3F_{2i-1} + F_{2i} +F_{2i-2})}{2} =  F_{2i} \\cdot F_{2i+1}.\\]\" width=\"484\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/4/0d402a3b42f8a9a3f4fbebf35e160be3e90c0d92.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c}  &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2ex] \\boldsymbol{i} &amp; 1 &amp; 2 &amp; 3 &amp; 4 &amp; 5 &amp; 6 &amp; 7 \\\\ [0.5ex] \\hline   &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-1.5ex]  \\boldsymbol{u_i} &amp; 1 &amp; 4 &amp; 11 &amp; 29 &amp; 76 &amp; 199 &amp; 521  \\\\ [1ex]      \\boldsymbol{v_i} &amp; 1 &amp; 2 &amp; 5 &amp; 13 &amp; 34 &amp; 89 &amp; 233 \\\\ [1ex]     \\boldsymbol{x_i} &amp; 2 &amp; 15 &amp; 104 &amp; 714 &amp; 4895 &amp; 33552 &amp; 229970 \\\\ [1ex]      \\boldsymbol{y_i} &amp; 1 &amp; 6 &amp; 40 &amp; 273 &amp; 1870 &amp; 12816 &amp; 87841 \\\\ [1ex]     \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"370\" height=\"147\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/5/1754089f89ed002e48b9f2059a54879964c63df1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\binom{15}{5} = \\binom{14}{6} =  3003\\]\" width=\"173\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/3/aa3dbbddd2a33e9c16093034657f220142ff6f8c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\binom{104}{39} = \\binom{103}{40} =  61218182743304701891431482520\\]\" width=\"418\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Equation_of_the_form_9\">Equation of the form</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pell%27s_equation_(simple_solutions)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Equation of the form\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018063232\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.053 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.065 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 742/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 35286/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in